<title>JAPAN: Sony&quot;s shares fall on profit-taking.</title>
<headline>Sony&quot;s shares fall on profit-taking.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Sony Corp eased on Wednesday morning, as participants continued to take profits in major international blue-chips after a recent buying spree, brokers said.</p>
<p>The share price of the consumer electronics giant fell 120 yen to 8,680 yen at 0047 GMT. Turnover was 556,100 shares.  </p>
<p>&quot;Sony is still the core of the market, and its shares will be bought again after a round of profit-taking,&quot; said a senior broker at a second-tier Japanese securities house.</p>
</text>
